{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/206","id":4699771780,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTfIvP88AAAABGCDThA","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/206","diff_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/206.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/206.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/206","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/206/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/206/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/issues/206/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/statuses/488e8f575a6c9bcc0bd097d2852c9a7fa19bf8a7","number":206,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"5100062: reviewed odd focal-inverse area-product proof","user":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Result\nClaimed full proof of k903,a for odd primitive periods, including permitted star traversals, in the strict nondegenerate confocal ellipse setting a > b > 0. The two polygons are obtained by unit-circle inversion of the ORIGINAL orbit vertices about the two ORIGINAL billiard foci. Their signed traversal-area product is constant.\n\nThe proof uses the classical genus-one Poncelet flag framework. Odd order separates the four common-tangent orbits; reversal lowers each focal area's apparent double poles to simple poles, while the opposite focal area vanishes there. The product is holomorphic on the compact flag curve. No conclusion from the separate k303,a target is assumed.\n\n## Exact sources and credit\n- [Reznik–Garcia–Koiller arXiv v11, Table 10 p. 12](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2004.12497v11) is the exact k903,a source. The shorter published Fifty New Invariants companion has no k903 row.\n- [The Talented Mr. Inversive Triangle](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.03020), Proposition 7 and Conjecture 1, credits the known N=3 case and states the general odd-period question.\n- [Chavez-Caliz](https://armj.math.stonybrook.edu/pdf-Springer-final/020-0154.pdf), p. 98, supplies the classical flag-curve framework.\n- The bicentric source DOI was corrected to [10.1007/s40598-021-00188-6](https://doi.org/10.1007/s40598-021-00188-6) and independently rechecked. No mathematical proof change was needed.\n\nNo novelty or priority claim.\n\n## Independent review\nSeparate full-target PASS for unchanged candidate SHA-256 `c4c2c5399d46f8aa30c4580160ea15a1375939eab3a2ba390d74abdce9a30905`. Review SHA-256 `966d99ee9c85a31dcd87713a0838d42c4aadf47719a732ea90184e769439b1c5`.\n\nAuthor controls: 91 exact assertions. Fresh independent controls: 3,553 exact assertions and 1,296 numerical diagnostics, including near-pole checks; author output replayed byte-for-byte. Numerical diagnostics are not interval certificates or the general proof.\n\n## Scope and accounting\nOnly the target attempt folder and its QUEUE row change, to claimed_solved at substantive author 1/5. Frozen pre-review files and their hashes are retained; PUBLICATION.md and PUBLICATION_STATUS.json give the later assessment. Downloaded PDFs, full extracted texts, source renders and private context are excluded. The unit normalization, original vertex/focus identities, signed-area convention and primitive odd scope are explicit.\n\nDraft for human review. No merge or release requested.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-01T05:36:26Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T05:36:26Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"AlecKriebel:dot/math-5100062","ref":"dot/math-5100062","repo":{"id":1307717439,"node_id":"R_kgDOTfIvPw","name":"Math","full_name":"AlecKriebel/Math","owner":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Alec's Math Explorations - provisional, unverified AI-assisted mathematics with exact verification artifacts.","homepage":"ht